{%- comment -%}
  An ordinary heading driven by one of the theme's ten text presets.

  **Not `title`, and the difference is the face.** `title` is `.display` — the
  oversized edge-to-edge section title, with its own gap rule against whatever
  follows it. This block is used inside a column of prose. A section wanting
  the editorial title treatment lists `title`; a section wanting a heading in
  running text lists this.

  **Size and level are two decisions, not one.** The size is a look and the
  level is the document's outline, and conflating them is how a page ends up
  with an `<h2>` wherever a large heading was wanted. rich-text's local block
  emitted `<h2>` whatever visual size was chosen. Preset and heading level are
  separate settings here, with the same guard against an arbitrary tag name as
  `blocks/title.liquid`.

  `"tag": null` because the block owns its element, as every text block here
  does — a generated wrapper would become the flex item in a `.stack` and the
  heading would stop being a sibling of the paragraphs it belongs with.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign heading_tag = block.settings.heading_level | default: 'h2'
  unless heading_tag == 'h1' or heading_tag == 'h2' or heading_tag == 'h3' or heading_tag == 'div'
    assign heading_tag = 'h2'
  endunless

  assign align_class = ''
  if block.settings.alignment != blank and block.settings.alignment != 'inherit'
    assign align_class = ' align-' | append: block.settings.alignment
  endif
-%}

{%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
  <{{ heading_tag }}
    class="h2{{ align_class }}"
    style="{% render 'text-style', preset: block.settings.style, font_style: block.settings.override_font, font_size: block.settings.override_size, color: block.settings.color, line_height: block.settings.override_leading, text_case: block.settings.override_case, letter_spacing: block.settings.override_tracking %}"
    {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
  >
    {{- block.settings.text -}}
  </{{ heading_tag }}>
{%- endif -%}

